---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Tendril from '../components/Tendril.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.webp';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who tends this garden, and the terms of the garden.">
  <section class="page-top about">
    <div class="bio">
      <h1 class="h1">The gardener</h1>
      <p>
        I came across an idea from Plotinus that I found very relatable. He said finding yourself is like a sculptor
        working on a block of marble. <span class="hl">You chip away everything that isn’t you, and what’s left is the real you.</span> It was there
        all along.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m trying to do that with my own life. Stripping out the expectations and “template life”, and figuring out which
        parts I actually want to keep.
      </p>
      <p>
        The question I ask myself is this: if nobody was watching and I didn’t have to keep doing it, would I still do it?
        Am I doing something just because everyone else is doing it, or does it really matter to me?
      </p>
      <p>It’s the opposite of <i lang="hi-Latn">log kya kahenge</i> (what will people say?).</p>
      <p>
        I’ve also noticed that the ideas I’ve absorbed come out fluent and clean. My own thoughts are clunky at first.
        They don’t roll off the tongue easily, because nobody has pre-packaged them for me. I usually get to my own
        stance only after a lot of questioning.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some things survive the chipping. For example, I’ve been a vegetarian all my life because of how I was raised.
        There’s no religious or moral reason behind it, for now at least. I’ve accepted it as part of who I am and eating
        meat doesn’t appeal to me. (Why vegetarian and not vegan, though? Still figuring that one out.)
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a garden of my thoughts, at different stages. Some are seeds, some are half-grown and some are nearly
        solidified. Take a look around, and feel free to engage with me (and challenge me) if something interests you.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Kavya smiling, in a pink floral dress, with plants behind her in black and white"
        width={680}
        widths={[340, 680]}
        sizes="340px"
        format="webp"
        quality={80}
        loading="eager"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><Tendril width={560} /></div>

  <section class="terms" aria-labelledby="terms-h">
    <h2 class="label" id="terms-h">Terms of the garden</h2>
    <p class="big">Everything here is a work in progress, including me.</p>
    <p>
      I reserve the right to be wrong, and to change my mind in public. Notes get rewritten without warning, and the dates
      show when.
    </p>
    <p>
      If something here helps you, borrow it, and say where it came from. If something's wrong, tell me. That's the whole
      point of tending things where people can see.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="more" aria-labelledby="more-h">
    <h2 class="h2" id="more-h">More of me</h2>
    <p>
      The <a class="kw-ul" href="/books">books that moved me</a>, my <a class="kw-ul" href="/done">reverse bucket list</a>,
      <a class="kw-ul" href="/experience">where I've worked</a>, <a class="kw-ul" href="/why">why the site looks like this</a>,
      and <a class="kw-ul" href="/thatha">a book about my grandfather</a> that I'm still finishing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hello">
    <h2 class="h2">Say hello</h2>
    <p>I read everything, slowly.</p>
    <p class="links">
      {site.socials.map((s) => <a class="kw-ul" href={s.href} rel="me">{s.label}</a>)}
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 40px 64px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .bio {
    flex: 999 1 28rem;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure-text);
    font-size: 18.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .bio .h1 {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .bio p + p {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .portrait {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    max-width: 340px;
  }
  .portrait :global(img) {
    display: block;
    border-radius: 10px;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .divider {
    margin: clamp(72px, 10vw, 112px) 0 clamp(40px, 6vw, 56px);
  }
  .terms {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .terms .label {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .terms .big {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'SOFT' 50, 'WONK' 1;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .terms p + p:not(.big) {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .more {
    max-width: var(--measure-text);
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .more .h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .more p {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .hello {
    max-width: var(--measure-text);
    margin-top: 56px;
  }
  .hello .h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 22px;
  }
  .links a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px 0;
    background-position: 0 calc(100% - 10px);
  }
</style>
